def LAD(*a): return list(a)
def RUB(a,b,c,d): return [(a,'Missing or unclear','Meets the stated check',b),(c,'Guessing','Evidence kept',d),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete and reviewed by a peer'),('Safety and ethics','Overlooked','Followed','Followed and taught to others')]
COURSES = [
dict(slug='mobile-apps-and-entertainment', title='Mobile Apps and Entertainment', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan, build and test a simple mobile app or entertainment product, measure how people use it, and bring it to a small group of users while respecting privacy and age rules.',
 outs=[('Define','the users and the need an app serves.'),('Apply','a screen flow and a simple no-code or low-code build.'),('Analyse','usage numbers to find where users leave.'),('Evaluate','privacy, age and content risks.'),('Create','a tested prototype and a launch note.')],
 task='Design, build and test a simple app prototype with five test users, then write a launch note with usage findings.', cond='About 10 weeks part-time. A phone, a computer, free no-code or low-code tools, five test users, a mentor.',
 standard='The need is written in one sentence, the prototype completes its main task in three taps or fewer, five users are tested and recorded, privacy risks are listed with fixes, and the launch note uses real numbers.', who='Students, hobby makers, freelancers, game and media enthusiasts, small business owners.', req='Comfort using a smartphone.',
 mods=[
 M('Find the user and the need','Define',4,['Describe one user by age, place, phone type and daily routine.','Write the need as one sentence: who wants what, and why.','Talk to five people and note their exact words.','Check that a free app does not already meet the need well.'],'Of 5 students interviewed in a hostel, 4 say they forget mess timings; the need is: students want mess timings on their phone lock screen.','Interview five people and write the need sentence.','Need sentence names the user, the goal and the reason, backed by five notes.','Why use the exact words of users?','They show the real problem and stop you from guessing.'),
 M('Choose the type of app','Analyse',4,['Compare a mobile web page, a no-code app and a native app on cost of time, skill and reach.','Note that low-end Android phones with 2 GB memory are common, so keep the app light.','Pick the simplest type that meets the need.','List what must work with weak internet.'],'A timings app of 6 screens is built as a no-code app of under 10 MB, which opens in 3 seconds on a 2 GB phone.','Write a one-page comparison and choose a type.','Choice is justified against need, skill and phone limits.','Why pick the simplest type?','It is faster to finish, test and fix.'),
 M('Sketch the screen flow','Create',5,['Draw each screen on paper with one main action.','Connect screens with arrows to show the path.','Keep the main task within three taps.','Use large buttons and text for small screens.'],'Flow: Home shows today\'s meals (1 tap), Tap meal shows menu (2 taps), Tap Remind sets an alert (3 taps).','Sketch a flow of five to seven screens.','Main task is reachable in three taps or fewer.','Why limit taps?','Fewer taps mean fewer people give up.'),
 M('Build a prototype','Apply',6,['Set up screens, buttons and a simple data list in a free tool.','Add one working feature, such as a list, a timer or a quiz.','Test on a real phone, not only on the computer.','Save a version before each big change.'],'A quiz app has 10 questions in a sheet, a score counter and a result screen; it runs on 3 different phones.','Build a prototype with one working feature.','The main task works on at least two real phones.','Why test on a real phone?','Screen size, speed and touch differ from the computer.'),
 M('Design for fun and clarity','Apply',4,['Give feedback for every action: a sound, a colour or a short message.','Use clear words, and offer Hindi or a local language if users prefer.','Check contrast so text is readable in sunlight.','Remove anything that does not help the main task.'],'Changing a grey button on white to dark blue on white raises contrast so 5 of 5 test users read it outdoors.','Improve three screens using the checks.','Each screen has feedback, clear words and readable contrast.','What is feedback in app design?','A sign that shows the app received the action.'),
 M('Test with real users','Evaluate',5,['Give five users one task and stay silent while they try.','Record time taken and where they hesitate.','Count how many finish without help.','Fix the top two problems and test again.'],'Round 1: 2 of 5 finish the task, average 95 seconds; after fixing the menu label, 4 of 5 finish in 40 seconds.','Run two test rounds with five users.','Completion rate and time are recorded for both rounds and improve.','Why stay silent during a test?','So you see what users really do without hints.'),
 M('Privacy, age and content rules','Evaluate',5,['Ask only for data the app needs and say why.','Follow India data protection rules and get parent or guardian consent when users are children.','Check ads, music, images and fonts for permission to use.','Write a short privacy note in plain words.'],'A quiz app drops the phone number field and keeps only a nickname, cutting stored personal data from 3 fields to 1.','Write a privacy note and a data list.','Every data field has a stated reason and content permissions are listed.','Why collect less data?','Less data means less harm if it is lost or misused.'),
 M('Capstone: launch note and usage review','Create',5,['Share the prototype with 15 users through a link or file.','Collect simple numbers: installs, opens in week one, users who finish the main task.','Find the screen where most users leave.','Write a launch note with findings and next steps.'],'Of 15 users, 12 open it, 9 finish the main task; 3 leave on the sign-in screen, so sign-in is removed.','Present the prototype and the launch note.','Note uses real counts, names one problem and gives one fix.','What does a drop-off point tell you?','Which screen to fix first.')],
 extra=[('Why keep an app small?','Many phones have little memory and slow internet.'),('Why save versions?','You can go back if a change breaks the app.')],
 rubric=RUB('Prototype','Main task works in three taps on real phones','Testing','Two rounds with recorded numbers that improve'),
 ladder=LAD('Use apps with awareness.','Explain how an app is planned.','Sketch flows and build a simple prototype.','Build, test and launch small apps alone.','Lead a small app team and review usage data.','Lead product quality and privacy across several apps.','Set product standards for a studio or a platform.'),
 jobs=['App maker','No-code developer','Junior product assistant','Game tester','Digital content producer']),

dict(slug='business-and-marketing', title='Business and Marketing Practice', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan a small business and market it with clear customers, offers, prices and measured results, using honest claims and simple numbers.',
 outs=[('Define','a customer, a need and an offer.'),('Apply','the marketing mix of product, price, place and promotion.'),('Analyse','sales and costs to find profit.'),('Evaluate','channels by cost per customer.'),('Create','a 90-day marketing plan.')],
 task='Build a one-page business plan and a 90-day marketing plan for a small venture, and run two weeks of measured marketing.', cond='About 10 weeks part-time. A real or practice business, a phone, a spreadsheet, a mentor.',
 standard='Claims are true, numbers are sourced, break-even is calculated, cost per customer is measured for at least two channels, and the plan has weekly measures.', who='Founders, shop owners, students, freelancers, home-based sellers.', req='Basic arithmetic.',
 mods=[
 M('Choose the customer and the need','Define',4,['Describe one customer by who, where, how often they buy and what they spend.','Write the need in the customer words.','Talk to ten likely customers and note what they pay now.','Name two alternatives the customer already uses.'],'A home tiffin seller targets office workers within 3 km who spend Rs 120 a day on lunch and want less oil.','Interview ten customers and write a customer profile.','Profile has place, spend, need and two alternatives.','Why name the alternatives?','Because you compete with what customers already do.'),
 M('Shape the offer','Create',5,['State what you sell, to whom, and the one reason to choose it.','Test the offer with ten people before building more.','Keep the first offer small: one product or one package.','Write a promise you can keep every time.'],'Offer: 5-day lunch box, fixed menu, delivered by 12:30; 6 of 10 people say they would try it for a week.','Write an offer and test it with ten people.','At least a stated share of testers would try it and the promise is specific.','Why keep the first offer small?','It is easier to deliver well and to learn from.'),
 M('Costs, price and break-even','Apply',6,['List fixed costs per month and variable cost per unit.','Set price from cost plus margin and compare with alternatives.','Calculate break-even units: fixed cost divided by price minus variable cost.','Check that price still leaves margin after discounts.'],'Fixed cost Rs 6,000 a month, price Rs 100, variable cost Rs 60; break-even is 6,000 / 40 = 150 boxes a month.','Calculate cost, price and break-even for your venture.','Break-even is shown with every cost line listed.','What does break-even tell you?','How many units you must sell to cover costs.'),
 M('The marketing mix','Apply',5,['Describe product, price, place and promotion in one line each.','Choose where customers can find and buy easily.','Pick promotion that fits the customer, such as a local group, a shop board or a short video.','Keep the four parts consistent with each other.'],'A budget snack seller places stalls near a coaching centre, prices at Rs 20, and promotes through a class group.','Write the mix for your offer.','All four parts are written and fit the customer.','Why must the four parts match?','A mismatch, like a premium price in a low-income area, loses sales.'),
 M('Honest messages and rules','Evaluate',4,['Make only claims you can prove, with a source.','Show price, quantity and conditions clearly.','Follow consumer protection and advertising rules in India.','Respect permission before sending messages to customers.'],'The claim best in town is changed to made fresh each morning, which you can show with a daily prep photo.','Rewrite five claims so each can be proved.','Each claim has evidence or is removed.','Why avoid claims you cannot prove?','They mislead customers and can break the law.'),
 M('Channels and cost per customer','Analyse',6,['Choose two channels to test, such as a messaging group and a flyer.','Track spend and new customers for each channel.','Divide spend by customers to get cost per customer.','Stop the costlier channel if results stay poor.'],'Flyers: Rs 500 spent, 5 customers, Rs 100 each. Messaging group: Rs 200 spent, 8 customers, Rs 25 each.','Run two channels for two weeks and compare.','Cost per customer is calculated for both channels.','How do you find cost per customer?','Spend on a channel divided by the customers it brought.'),
 M('Sales, repeat buyers and feedback','Evaluate',4,['Count sales per week and the share who buy again.','Ask each customer one question after purchase.','Note complaints and fix the most common one.','Compare actual sales with your break-even.'],'Of 40 customers, 14 bought again within 30 days, a repeat rate of 35%.','Collect feedback and repeat data from 20 customers.','Repeat rate and top complaint are recorded.','Why track repeat buyers?','They cost less than new customers and show real satisfaction.'),
 M('Capstone: 90-day plan','Create',5,['Write the one-page business plan with customer, offer, price and break-even.','Set weekly targets for sales and cost per customer.','Plan the budget by channel and week.','List risks and what you will do if sales fall short.'],'Target: 150 boxes a month by week 8, marketing spend capped at Rs 1,500, reviewed every Sunday.','Present the plan and two weeks of results.','Plan has weekly numbers and results are compared with targets.','What makes a plan measurable?','Weekly numbers you can compare with results.')],
 extra=[('Why test an offer before scaling?','It shows demand before you spend much.'),('Why review numbers every week?','Problems are caught early, while they are cheap to fix.')],
 rubric=RUB('Plan','Customer, offer, price and break-even all stated with numbers','Measurement','Cost per customer tracked weekly for each channel'),
 ladder=LAD('Know basic business words.','Explain customer, offer and price.','Cost and price a small offer.','Run and market a small venture alone.','Lead a team and a marketing budget.','Lead marketing strategy across products.','Set strategy and standards for a business unit.'),
 jobs=['Small business owner','Marketing assistant','Sales executive','Digital marketing associate','Business development associate']),

dict(slug='personal-wellness', title='Personal Wellness Coaching', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Build habits for sleep, movement, food and mind, and coach others honestly within clear limits, without medical claims.',
 outs=[('Define','the pillars of wellness and the limits of a coach.'),('Apply','habit-building steps with a client.'),('Analyse','a client habit log.'),('Evaluate','claims, risks and when to refer.'),('Create','a four-week habit plan.')],
 task='Coach one volunteer through a four-week habit plan with a log, weekly reviews and a referral check.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. One adult volunteer, a habit log, a mentor.',
 standard='Advice stays inside coach limits, risks are referred to a qualified professional, consent is recorded, and progress is shown by a weekly habit log.', who='Wellness enthusiasts, teachers, fitness staff, community volunteers.', req='Willingness to listen without judging.',
 mods=[
 M('The pillars and the coach limits','Define',4,['Name the pillars: sleep, movement, food, mind and social connection.','State that a coach supports habits and does not diagnose, treat or prescribe.','List signs that need a doctor, such as chest pain, fainting or long low mood.','Write your limits on a one-page scope note.'],'Scope note: I help set sleep and walking habits; I do not advise on medicines, diseases or diets for illness.','Write a scope note and a referral list.','Note lists what you do, what you never do and who to refer to.','Why state coach limits?','They protect the client and keep advice safe.'),
 M('Start with listening and consent','Apply',4,['Ask open questions about the day, energy and what the client wants.','Get written consent for coaching and for keeping notes.','Ask about health conditions and ask the client to check with a doctor before changing exercise.','Keep notes private.'],'Intake asks: What would a good week look like? The client wants to feel less tired by 4 pm and signs consent.','Run an intake with a volunteer.','Consent and goals are recorded, with a doctor check noted where needed.','Why get consent first?','It respects the client choice and privacy.'),
 M('Set small and clear goals','Create',5,['Turn a wish into a small action with a number: walk 15 minutes after dinner, 5 days a week.','Attach the habit to an existing routine, such as after brushing teeth.','Pick one habit at a time.','Agree how it will be logged.'],'Goal: lights out by 11 pm on 5 of 7 nights, set after the client finishes tea at 10 pm.','Write two goals in this format.','Each goal has action, number, days and a trigger.','Why start with one habit?','Too many changes at once usually fail.'),
 M('Sleep and daily movement','Apply',5,['Explain that many adults need about seven to nine hours of sleep.','Suggest a steady sleep time and less screen use before bed.','Suggest short walks and stretching built into the day, with the client pace.','Stop and refer if pain or dizziness appears.'],'Client moves from 5 hours 30 minutes sleep to 6 hours 30 minutes in two weeks by sleeping 30 minutes earlier each week.','Plan a sleep and movement habit.','Plan uses gradual steps and a stop rule.','What do you do if movement causes pain?','Stop and advise the client to see a doctor.'),
 M('Food and water habits','Apply',5,['Support simple habits: more vegetables, regular meals, enough water, less sugary drinks.','Use local home foods and the client budget and culture.','Do not give diet plans for illness, or promise weight results.','Refer to a qualified dietitian for medical needs.'],'Habit: one fruit or vegetable portion added to lunch on 5 days, replacing one sweet drink a day.','Plan a food habit for a volunteer.','Habit uses local foods and avoids medical claims.','Why avoid promising weight results?','Results vary by person and promises can mislead.'),
 M('Stress and mind habits','Apply',4,['Teach one simple practice, such as slow breathing for two minutes or a short daily note of three good things.','Encourage talking with trusted people and keeping a routine.','Listen without judging and avoid giving advice on mental illness.','Know the helpline and refer when someone speaks of harming themselves.'],'A 2-minute breathing break at 3 pm is logged on 4 of 5 workdays and the client reports feeling calmer.','Practise a stress habit with a partner.','Practice is simple and a referral route is named.','When must you refer immediately?','When someone may harm themselves or is in crisis.'),
 M('Read the habit log','Analyse',4,['Count the days each habit was done out of the days planned.','Find the day or time when the habit usually fails.','Ask what got in the way before suggesting change.','Adjust the habit to be easier, not harder.'],'Walking logged 3 of 5 planned days; both misses were rainy evenings, so a 10-minute indoor option is added.','Analyse four weeks of a log.','Findings name a pattern and one small change.','Why make a habit easier when it fails?','Easy habits are more likely to continue.'),
 M('Capstone: four-week plan','Create',5,['Complete intake, scope note and consent.','Set one habit per week with a weekly review call.','Keep the log and a short note after each review.','Write a final summary with results and next steps.'],'Four weeks: 18 of 24 planned habit days done (75%), sleep up by 50 minutes, and one referral advised for back pain.','Present the plan, log and summary.','Log is complete, advice stays within limits and referrals are recorded.','What shows progress honestly?','The log of habit days done, not promises of results.')],
 extra=[('Why keep client notes private?','Health information is personal and trust depends on it.'),('Why celebrate small wins?','They build confidence to keep the habit going.')],
 rubric=RUB('Coaching limits','Scope note followed with no diagnosis or treatment advice','Habit tracking','Weekly log reviewed with the client and used to adjust'),
 ladder=LAD('Look after your own habits.','Explain the pillars of wellness.','Support a friend with one habit.','Coach clients alone within limits.','Lead a group wellness programme.','Lead wellness programmes across a community or workplace.','Set standards for ethical coaching across organisations.'),
 jobs=['Wellness coach','Community health volunteer','Fitness assistant','Workplace wellness facilitator','Wellness programme coordinator']),
]
